    <section class="main_banner position-relative am-extra-banner" style="background-image: url('assets/img/bg/prayer_bg.jpg');">
        <div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12 text-center"><span class="am-extra-eyebrow">Al-Asim Quran &bull; Islamic Education</span><h1>Pillars of Islam</h1><p><a href="Default.aspx">Home</a> <i class="fa-solid fa-angles-right"></i> Pillars of Islam</p></div></div></div>
    </section>
    <section class="am-pillars-content section-padding">
        <div class="container">
            <header class="am-pillars-intro text-center wow fadeInUp"><span class="am-tajweed-eyebrow">Foundation of a Muslim’s Faith</span><h2>The Five Pillars that Shape Islamic Life and Belief</h2><p>The Pillars of Islam are central acts of worship and practice. They guide a Muslim’s faith, relationship with Allah (SWT), and responsibilities in daily life.</p></header>
            <div class="row g-4">
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6"><article class="am-pillar-card"><span class="am-pillar-number">01</span><span class="am-pillar-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-star-and-crescent"></i></span><h3>Shahadah <small>Faith</small></h3><p>The declaration of faith affirms that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad ﷺ is His messenger. It is the foundation of a Muslim’s belief.</p></article></div>
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6"><article class="am-pillar-card"><span class="am-pillar-number">02</span><span class="am-pillar-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-person-praying"></i></span><h3>Salah <small>Prayer</small></h3><p>Muslims perform five daily prayers at their prescribed times. Salah is an act of worship and a regular connection with Allah.</p></article></div>
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6"><article class="am-pillar-card"><span class="am-pillar-number">03</span><span class="am-pillar-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-hand-holding-heart"></i></span><h3>Zakat <small>Charity</small></h3><p>Zakat is the required giving of a prescribed portion of qualifying wealth to eligible recipients. It supports those in need and encourages care for the community.</p></article></div>
                <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-6"><article class="am-pillar-card"><span class="am-pillar-number">04</span><span class="am-pillar-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-moon"></i></span><h3>Sawm <small>Fasting</small></h3><p>Fasting during Ramadan is an act of worship that nurtures self-discipline, patience, gratitude and compassion for people facing hardship.</p></article></div>
                <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-6"><article class="am-pillar-card"><span class="am-pillar-number">05</span><span class="am-pillar-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-kaaba"></i></span><h3>Hajj <small>Pilgrimage</small></h3><p>Hajj is the pilgrimage to Makkah required once in a lifetime for Muslims who are physically and financially able. It brings worshippers together from across the world.</p></article></div>
            </div>
